<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diodotus II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diodotus II was the second king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-bactrian-kingdom">Greco-Bactrian Kingdom</a>, son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diodotus-i">Diodotus I</a>, ruling in the later 3rd century BCE. He is reported to have made an alliance with the Parthian ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsaces-i">Arsaces I</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucids</a>. He was overthrown and killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euthydemus-i">Euthydemus I</a>, who founded a new dynasty around 225 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diodotus-ii.jpg" alt="Diodotus II" width="252" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group (uploaded by Udimu) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Diodotos_II_(croped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
